nfidelities into poetry.Doji Retsuo — Older brother. The model heir. Thinks she is too verbose.Doji Emika — Younger sister. Sees Setsuna as a woman trapped by duty, but keeps her thoughts private. Has no desire to follow in her footsteps. Reserved in Setsuna's plans for the Toshi Ranbo settlement, to marry into the Matsu family and satisfy the grandmother's restoration demand.Matsu Tomoe — Late maternal grandmother. Married into the Crane from the Matsu and hated being a Crane for the rest of her life. Now haunts Setsuna as a ghost, demanding the restoration of Toshi Ranbo and the Matsu lineage.Marriage\nShinjō Harunobu — Husband. A respected Shinjō commander, currently a Lion prisoner of war. Loves her and respects her intellect, though he considers her work legal trickery and prefers to solve problems directly. He understands he has married up. They communicate by letter; the marriage has been long-distance for years.Mentors and Superiors\nBayushi Tomono — Scorpion courtier she encountered in Shirogome. Engaged her in wordplay and taught her how to exploit Imperial law and weaponize harmlessness. One of three people whose approval she cares about.Asahina Shigehiro — Her former lord, Crane shugenja and ruler of the city of Shirogome. Employed her as legal counsel on matters of Imperial law. One of three whose approval matters.Kitsuki Kāgi — Her Emerald Magistrate superior. Recruited her into Imperial service after the Kakita tax loophole brought her to his attention. One of three whose approval matters.Magistrate Colleagues\nKakita Kazumi — Kakita duelist, Topaz Champion, and trained Crane Harrier (shinobi) operating in plain sight. Has consistently shown her discretion and quiet loyalty, including providing logistical support during the abortion procedure.Shiba Midori — Phoenix shugenja. Brewed the abortifacient and conducted the procedure. The sole peer-level intimate with whom Setsuna has been visibly unmasked. Her shugenja presence first allowed the grandmother's ghost to manifest.Lord\nMiya Misato — Imperial Envoy, sixteen years old. Originally dispatched on a mission designed to fail. Setsuna appointed herself as her advisor and has invested her own XP transferring skills to her. Nearly assassinated and now blind, but alive. The displaced object of the motherhood Setsuna refused, and simultaneously her operational frame and political instrument.Adversary\nKakita Noritomo — The Kakita provincial daimyō whose new artisan tax Setsuna voided through an Imperial precedent during her time in Shirogome. He banned her from his lands rather than risk a contest he would lose; the institutional grudge remains active in the Kakita family.The Lover At Court\nAn unnamed member of an Imperial family in Otosan Uchi. Father of the pregnancy Setsuna conceived approximately four months before her departure for Loyalty Castle. He does not know she was pregnant and has never known. Setsuna does not pursue contact."
